//Aim
To connect Tableau to a data source and prepare the data for creating visualizations.

//Algorithm
1. Open Tableau Public.
2. Select the required data source.
3. Import the dataset.
4. Verify the imported data.
5. Perform basic data preparation.
6. Save the workbook.

Program
1 import pandas as pd
2
3 # Load dataset
4 data = pd.read_csv("sales_data.csv")
5
6 # Display first 5 rows
7 print(data.head())
8
9 # Check for missing values
10 print(data.isnull().sum())
11
12 # Remove duplicate records
13 data = data.drop_duplicates()
14
15 # Convert Sales column to numeric
16 data["Sales"] = pd.to_numeric(data["Sales"])
18 # Save cleaned dataset
19 data.to_csv("cleaned_sales_data.csv", index=False)
20
21 print("Data prepared successfully.")

//Sample Output
The output displays the first five rows, missing-value counts and a confirmation that the cleaned
dataset was saved successfully.

//Result
Thus, the dataset was successfully connected, cleaned, and prepared for visualization using
